https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1344693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomfull123","html_url":"https://github.com/tomfull123","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomfull123/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomfull123/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomfull123/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomfull123/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomfull123/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomfull123/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomfull123/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomfull123/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tomfull123/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-26T14:24:48Z","updated_at":"2025-04-26T14:24:48Z","body":"> Supporting `Object *` and `Ref` in `TypedArray` definitely makes sense to me.\r\n> \r\n> But I'm not sure if simply removing the pointer is a sufficiently safe implementation. We don't want to accidentally support `TypedArray<int64_t *>` with `int64_t` values. Perhaps there's a way to narrow it down more safely?\r\n\r\nI'm pretty sure that `int64_t *` would error either way since `int64_t` doesn't have the `get_class_static()` method, this change just makes it so we can call `get_class_static()` on pointer template types too","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2832243476/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]